.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt NDI_EVENT_DEFINITION 9S
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndi_event_definition ,
.Nm ndi_event_definition_t
.Nd nexus event definition
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sunndi.h
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos specific
.Pq Consolidation Private .
.Sh DESCRIPTION
An \fBndi_event_definition_t\fP describes an event supplied by a nexus driver.
An array of these structures is referenced by an \fBndi_event_set_t\fP and bound
to an event handle with \fBndi_event_bind_set()\fP.
The framework keeps pointers to the definitions and their names instead of
copying them.
Keep both valid and unchanged for as long as any bound cookie refers to them.
Static driver storage is suitable.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va ndi_event_tag
Nexus-assigned integer used by the event conversion functions.
Use distinct tags within a handle and avoid the value \fBNDI_FAILURE\fP, which
is the failure result of \fBndi_event_cookie_to_tag()\fP.
.It Va ndi_event_name
Null-terminated event name used for cookie lookup.
Names must be distinct within a handle.
.It Va ndi_event_plevel
Execution level: \fBEPL_KERNEL\fP, \fBEPL_INTERRUPT\fP, or \fBEPL_HIGHLEVEL\fP.
The producer and callbacks must obey the restrictions of that level, and the
handle locks must be initialized with an appropriate interrupt block cookie.
A handle cannot mix \fBEPL_HIGHLEVEL\fP events with other levels.
.It Va ndi_event_attributes
Use \fBNDI_EVENT_POST_TO_ALL\fP to deliver to every registration or
\fBNDI_EVENT_POST_TO_TGT\fP to restrict delivery to the specified child.
\fBNDI_EVENT_POST_TO_ALL\fP is zero, not an independently testable flag bit.
\fBndi_event_do_callback()\fP overrides this selection and invokes a single
matching registration.
.El
.Sh STRUCTURE MEMBERS
.Bd -literal -offset indent
int             ndi_event_tag;
char            *ndi_event_name;
ddi_plevel_t    ndi_event_plevel;
uint_t          ndi_event_attributes;
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ndi_event_add_callback 9F ,
.Xr ndi_event_alloc_hdl 9F ,
.Xr ndi_event_retrieve_cookie 9F ,
.Xr ndi_event_set 9S
